{"BlockedEmail.should_block? increments match_count and updates last_match_at inside EmailValidator#validate_each, causing stats to be incremented multiple times per signup attempt when valid? is called more than once": 0.7494324445724487, "rejectedEmails defined on prototype is shared across all CreateAccountController instances, causing rejected emails from one session to persist and incorrectly block submission in subsequent sessions": 0.6565666198730469, "result.values.email can be undefined/null but is not guarded before pushing into rejectedEmails, causing undefined/null to be added and incorrectly blocking future submissions with falsy email values": 0.35193443298339844, "InviteRedeemer bypasses BlockedEmail validation - create_new_user has no error handling to check if user was saved or inspect validation errors, allowing blocked users to register via invite links": 0.5361967086791992, "In Rails 3, email_changed? returns false for new unsaved records, causing validates :email with if: :email_changed? to skip BlockedEmail check on every new signup": 0.3130022883415222, "Error response leaks user attribute values (name, username, email) to the client, allowing attackers to probe whether specific emails are blocked and potentially enabling reflected attacks": 0.4630674719810486, "Blocked email shows generic 'invalid' error message (user.email.invalid) instead of 'blocked' message (user.email.blocked), misleading users about why their email was rejected": 0.7157824635505676}